---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icons from "../../components/Icons.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Summer Palace vs Beihai Park: Which Imperial Garden Should You Visit?" description="Summer Palace or Beihai Park? Compare the two imperial gardens — scale, lake experiences, crowds, and best visit times. Honest verdict on which royal garden fits your itinerary.">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "Compare", href: "/#compare-guides" }, { label: "Summer Palace vs Beihai Park" }]} />
  <div class="relative py-24 md:py-32 overflow-hidden -mt-[68px]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center" style="background-image:url('/images/attractions/beihai-park.webp')"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#0a3b36]/88"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 text-center">
      <span class="tag tag-glass mb-4">Compare & Decide</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">Summer Palace vs Beihai Park</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 mx-auto max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/80">Two imperial lakeside gardens — one vast, one intimate. Which one belongs in your day?</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 pb-6">
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#0f766e] pl-5 py-2 rounded-r bg-[#ccfbf1]/30">
      <p class="text-base text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">The short answer:</strong> Choose the <strong>Summer Palace</strong> for the full imperial-garden experience — its scale, the Long Corridor, and Kunming Lake make it the definitive royal garden and a half-day destination. Choose <strong>Beihai Park</strong> for a beautiful 2-hour lakeside escape in the middle of the old city, perfect to chain with Jingshan and the Forbidden City. Ideally do both — they sit on opposite sides of the city and serve different days.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Side-by-Side Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[#d5d0c4] rounded-xl">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-[#f8f7f4] text-[#5c5a4c] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Feature</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Summer Palace</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Beihai Park</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Size</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">716 acres (290 ha)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">~170 acres (69 ha)</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Ticket</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">CNY 20-30 combined</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">CNY 10</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Time needed</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">3-4 hours (half-day)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">1.5-2 hours</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Location</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Haidian, NW — 40 min from center</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Xicheng, central old city</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Centerpiece</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Tower of Buddhist Incense + Long Corridor</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">White Dagoba on Jade Mountain</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Boat rides</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Lake cruises + pedal boats</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Pedal/rowing boats</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Crowds</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Moderate, bus tours at East Gate</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Lighter, more local</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Combine with</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Old Summer Palace ruins</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Jingshan, Forbidden City, Drum Towers</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Seasonal star</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Spring magnolias, summer lake</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Winter skating on the frozen lake</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">The Core Difference</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#d5d0c4]/40 p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-2">The Summer Palace is a destination</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed">It is a full imperial garden built on the grandest scale — a dedicated journey out of the city to spend half a day wandering its lake and hill. The Long Corridor alone (728 meters of painted galleries) is worth the trip, and the boat ride across Kunming Lake with the Tower of Buddhist Incense rising behind you is one of Beijing's great set pieces. You plan a day around it, and it repays the investment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#d5d0c4]/40 p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-2">Beihai Park is an interlude</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed">Beihai is the imperial garden you slip into for an hour or two between the big sights. It sits right in the old city, its White Dagoba is instantly photogenic, and it moves at a human pace — locals fishing, tai chi, kite-flying, rowboats on the lake. It is easier, cheaper, and quieter than the Summer Palace, and in winter its frozen lake becomes Beijing's most beloved skating rink. Not a destination to plan a day around; a pleasure to find on a walking day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Which One Is Right for You?</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="clock" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Want the definitive imperial garden?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Summer Palace. It is the largest and best-preserved imperial garden in China, and the only one that feels like a full destination.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="map-pin" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Central location a priority?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Beihai Park. It is a 10-minute walk from Jingshan and a short walk from the Forbidden City and Drum Towers — no half-hour metro ride required.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="heart" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Short on time?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Beihai. Two hours covers the dagoba, the lake, and the pavilions. The Summer Palace demands at least half a day.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="star" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Visiting in winter?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Beihai Park, hands down — skating on the frozen lake is a Beijing institution. The Summer Palace's lake freezes too but Beihai's central location and local atmosphere make it the classic choice.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8 border-t border-[#edeae3] pt-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Our Verdict by Traveler Type</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[#d5d0c4] rounded-xl">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-[#f8f7f4] text-[#5c5a4c] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">If you are...</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Pick</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Want THE imperial garden</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Summer Palace</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Largest, most complete, iconic</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Only 2 hours to spare</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Beihai Park</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Quick, central, satisfying</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">With kids</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Beihai Park</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Easy walk, boats, ice skating</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Photographer</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Summer Palace</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Bigger compositions, lake + pagoda</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Chaining a central day</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Beihai Park</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Slots between Forbidden City + Jingshan</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Winter visit</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Beihai Park</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">The classic skating experience</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Do Both Without Overlapping</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed mb-4">They actually fit different days. Beihai Park belongs on your central old-city day — Forbidden City, Jingshan, Beihai, and the Drum Towers make a brilliant walking loop. The Summer Palace belongs on a half-day of its own, usually paired with the Old Summer Palace ruins or simply taken slowly by the lake. Doing both means two distinct, complementary garden experiences — neither one is a lesser version of the other.</p>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#fef3c7] border border-[#d4a373]/30 p-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">The honest bottom line:</strong> if you can only pick one garden, pick the Summer Palace — it is the definitive version. But Beihai Park is not a compromise; it is the smarter choice on a day already packed with the central sights. Both are worth your time, and most Beijing itineraries benefit from including both.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
